  "body": "## What changed\n\nTry Solidcore's constrained mesher when its display planner leaves a face above the chord tolerance.\nKeep all existing acceptance checks.\nAdd the reported STEP and Solidcraft fixtures with regression tests.\nRecord the raw display-mesh result in the STEP agreement bench.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe display planner reaches its refinement limit on the stepped cylindrical face.\nIt reports face 12 at 3.306568 mm sag for a 0.005 mm tolerance.\nThe machining importer refuses that plan before trying another mesher.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `hole_on_pocket_wall_meshes_within_tolerance`\n- `hole_on_pocket_wall_solidcraft_meshes_within_tolerance`\n\nBoth pins fail on unchanged `upstream/main` at `6679b1b4b`.\nBoth pass with the fix.\nThey check the 0.005 mm continuous bound, a closed mesh, 13 faces and the analytic volume within 1 mm³.\nMutation: restore `machining_mesh.rs` from `upstream/main`; both pins fail with the reported capped face.\nRestore the fix; both pins pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed 96 of 97 steps.\nThe new fixture required an agreement-bench inventory entry.\nAfter that expected extension, the failed-step gate retry passed all 29 agreement tests.\nAll other selected geometry, kernel, app and UI steps passed.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed after the final test edits.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` files changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe full release gate and manual GUI import were not run.\nThe raw display planner still gives this fixture an incorrect area.\nThe machining importer now uses the checked fallback.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. The changed files have no open PR overlap.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Import STEP and Solidcraft models with a hole on a pocket wall through a checked meshing fallback.\n\nFixes #3444\n",
